  "narrative": {
    "intro": "It Concepts obligated $247M in FY2026 to date across 19 awards, with an average award size of $13M. Obligations are down 1.1% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer, accounting for $180M of obligations, while Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market at $217M. Fiscal-year detail shows a growth path from $34.5M in FY21 to $155M in FY22, $137M in FY23, $264M in FY24, $249M in FY25, and $247M in FY26. The General Services Administration and the Social Security Administration are secondary buyers, at $28.9M and $28.2M respectively. The mix of large awards and a single dominant customer points to concentration risk concentrated in computer systems work. That concentration matters for revenue stability and for where business development effort should focus next, especially among the top buying agencies and markets listed here.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are It Concepts’ federal obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs accounts for $180M of the $247M total, which shows strong customer concentration. The Computer Systems Design Services market accounts for $217M, which shows sector concentration by NAICS. Those two concentrations together mean a small number of agencies and one primary market drive most obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and markets drive It Concepts’ FY2026 to date results?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs, General Services Administration, and Social Security Administration are the top buyers at $180M, $28.9M, and $28.2M respectively. The top markets are Computer Systems Design Services at $217M and Engineering Services at $28.9M. Several buyers and markets outside the top ranks show minimal or negative entries without material totals."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does It Concepts make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "It Concepts has $247M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. It Concepts obtained those obligations across 19 awards, with an average award size of $13M, and obligations are down 1.1% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from It Concepts?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, with $180M in obligations. Other significant buyers include the General Services Administration at $28.9M and the Social Security Administration at $28.2M, followed by the Department of Defense at $6.9M, the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau at $2M, and the Department of Commerce at $905K."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does It Concepts sell to the government?",
